Concept
  1.A custom error is a way to define our own error in a Solidity contract.
  2.Instead of writing a long error message every time, we can create an error with a name and use it when needed.
  3.Custom errors are also more **gas-efficient** than string error messages.

Syntax

error ErrorName();

To use it:

revert ErrorName();

Example

// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
pragma solidity ^0.8.20;

contract CustomErrorExample {

    error InsufficientBalance();

    uint public balance = 100;

    function withdraw(uint amount) public {
        if (amount > balance) {
            revert InsufficientBalance();
        }

        balance -= amount;
    }
}


Use case :

* We can create our own error using "error".
* Custom errors are used with "revert".
* They make error handling more clear.
* They usually use less gas than long error strings.
